              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't want to put these on the grill in the rain, so I followed the directions exactly and put them in a 400 degree oven for 1 hour. Delicious! The onions were full of flavor, but the potatoes needed a little more salt. Easy enough to do."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was great!!! Full of flavor! And a snap to pull together!! I don’t have wooden slotted spoons so had to freehand/approximate the slices and how far down. My husband also grilled on med heat, which meant the cooking time was darn close but some of my onions (chopped) were a little burnt. Nonetheless! Delicious side to our all-grilled meal. Thank you! Will make again this summer!!",
